-- title:
--   Proposition 4.3 — Simultaneous Gaussian evaluation independence
-- statement:
--   For every $n,d\in\mathbb N$, there exists a Borel set $\mathcal X_{n,d}\subset(\mathbb R^d)^n$ with Lebesgue-null complement such that, for every $x\in\mathcal X_{n,d}$, every $k\in\mathbb N$ with $k(d+1)\le n$, and every injective list $\theta:\{1,\ldots,k\}\to\mathbb R^d$, the columns of the matrix $(\phi_d(x_i-\theta_j))_{i,j}$ are linearly independent over $\mathbb R$, where $\phi_d(y)=(2\pi)^{-d/2}e^{-\|y\|^2/2}$. The conull set is chosen before the location list, so the locations may depend on the data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/hanshengjiang/reweighted-npmle-lean/blob/5af8d16822c5a8a3f032b13eb95daea40f307484/ReweightedNPMLE/GaussianGenericity.lean#L99-L119

